window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-f8889c3a5e0f278c"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"fix-a-finding-from-your-security-scan\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"_1\">修复安全扫描发现的问题</h1> <p>打开扫描发现项，审查并应用补丁，然后验证修复结果。</p> <p>使用 Codex Security 插件，将已审查的扫描发现项转成有针对性的补丁。在本地检查并应用更改、验证修复，然后准备附有证据的拉取请求。</p> <p><a id=\"best-for\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">适合哪些情况</h2> <ul> <li>准备处理 Codex Security 扫描中已审查发现项的开发者。</li> <li>希望先检查拟议补丁，再在本地应用的维护者。</li> <li>希望在有针对性的安全修复旁边一并审查验证证据的审查者。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"skills-plugins\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">技能与插件</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>技能或插件</th> <th>用途</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-44471eb3eae1b363\">$codex-security:fix-finding</a></td> <td>使用有针对性的补丁和验证证据，修复并验证一项经过审查的安全发现。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a id=\"related-links\"></a></td> <td></td> </tr> <tr> <td>## 关联文档</td> <td></td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-8531f28e6406b574\">运行首次安全扫描</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-44471eb3eae1b363\">修复并验证安全发现项</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-fa2e3549e489b26b\">修复漏洞积压事项</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"before-you-start\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">开始之前</h2> <p>在 Codex 中打开已安装并启用 <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/docs/security/plugin\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Codex Security 插件（需联网）</a>的受扫描代码库。你需要先审查过某项发现，并决定要处理它。如果还没有运行扫描，请从<a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/use-cases/find-vulnerabilities-in-your-code\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">运行首次安全扫描（需联网）</a>开始。</p> <p><a id=\"fix-the-finding\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">修复发现项</h2> <ol> <li>打开并审查发现项</li> </ol> <p>在 <strong>Findings（发现项）</strong> 或 <strong>Scans（扫描）</strong> 中打开某项发现。阅读受影响的代码、报告的影响以及支持该发现的证据。</p> <p>确认修复应阻止什么情况，以及哪些正常行为必须继续有效。如果证据不清楚，请先调查该发现，再着手修改。</p> <ol> <li>生成有针对性的补丁</li> </ol> <p>选择 <strong>Patch（补丁）</strong> 标签页，然后选择 <strong>Generate patch（生成补丁）</strong>。</p> <p>在可行时，Codex 会验证或复现问题，并生成拟议补丁。生成补丁不会修改你选定的工作副本。</p> <ol> <li>审查并应用补丁</li> </ol> <p>检查拟议差异，包括回归测试或验证制品。确认更改解决了该发现，并且保留预期行为。继续之前，先处理无关更改或范围更大的重构。</p> <p>补丁准备就绪后，选择 <strong>Apply patch（应用补丁）</strong>。然后审查工作树中的差异。</p> <pre><code> &lt;figcaption className=\"mt-3 text-sm text-secondary\"&gt;\n   安全文档中的补丁示例，并非实际执行本指南后生成的结果。应用之前，请审查你自己的差异。\n &lt;/figcaption&gt;\n</code></pre> <ol> <li>验证修复</li> </ol> <p>选择 <strong>Verify fix（验证修复）</strong>。</p> <p>审查证据，确认原先存在漏洞的行为已无法复现，同时正常行为仍可工作。在安全且可行时，有针对性的回归测试应当在修复前失败、修复后通过。</p> <p>如果验证不完整，请检查其中说明的限制，并确定还需要哪些测试。仅仅应用补丁并不能证明漏洞已经修复。</p> <ol> <li>准备更改以供审查</li> </ol> <p>审查最终差异，并按照常规开发流程准备拉取请求。请包含：</p> <ul> <li>发现项，以及补丁要纠正的行为。</li> <li>相关代码更改。</li> <li>验证命令及其结果。</li> <li>仍存在的不确定性或后续测试。</li> </ul> <p>验证不会自动关闭该发现项。请根据团队的审查和发布流程，主动更新其状态。</p> <p><a id=\"review-the-result\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_6\">审查结果</h2> <p>最终应得到一个范围明确的补丁、说明 Codex 验证了什么的证据，以及足够的信息供其他人审查。如果验证无法证明修复有效，请明确保留这一缺口。</p> <p>有关更多详情，请参阅<a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/docs/security/plugin/fix-findings\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">修复并验证安全发现项（需联网）</a>。如果要处理现有报告或工单，请参阅<a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/use-cases/remediate-vulnerability-backlog\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">修复漏洞积压事项（需联网）</a>。</p>","en":"<h1 id=\"fix-a-finding-from-your-security-scan\">Fix a finding from your security scan</h1> <p>Open a finding from your scan, review and apply a patch, and verify the fix.</p> <p>Use the Codex Security plugin to turn a reviewed scan finding into a focused patch. Review and apply the change locally, verify the fix, and prepare a pull request with supporting evidence.</p> <h2 id=\"best-for\">Best for</h2> <ul> <li>Developers ready to address a reviewed finding from a Codex Security scan.</li> <li>Maintainers who want to inspect a proposed patch before applying it locally.</li> <li>Reviewers who need verification evidence alongside a focused security fix.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"skills-plugins\">Skills &amp; Plugins</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Skill or plugin</th> <th>Why use it</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-44471eb3eae1b363\">$codex-security:fix-finding</a></td> <td>Fix and verify one reviewed security finding with a focused patch and validation evidence.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>## Related links</td> <td></td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-8531f28e6406b574\">Run your first security scan</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-44471eb3eae1b363\">Fix and verify security findings</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-fa2e3549e489b26b\">Remediate a vulnerability backlog</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"before-you-start\">Before you start</h2> <p>Open the scanned repository in Codex with the <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/docs/security/plugin\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Codex Security plugin (online)</a> installed and enabled. You'll need a finding you've reviewed and decided to address. If you haven't run a scan yet, start with <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/use-cases/find-vulnerabilities-in-your-code\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Run your first security scan (online)</a>.</p> <h2 id=\"fix-the-finding\">Fix the finding</h2> <ol> <li>Open and review the finding</li> </ol> <p>Open the finding from <strong>Findings</strong> or a completed scan in <strong>Scans</strong>. Read the affected code, the reported impact, and the evidence supporting the finding.</p> <p>Confirm what the fix should prevent and which legitimate behavior must continue to work. If the evidence is unclear, investigate the finding before moving to a patch.</p> <ol> <li>Generate a focused patch</li> </ol> <p>Select the <strong>Patch</strong> tab, then <strong>Generate patch</strong>.</p> <p>Codex validates or reproduces the issue when feasible and generates a proposed patch. Generating the patch does not modify your selected checkout.</p> <ol> <li>Review and apply the patch</li> </ol> <p>Inspect the proposed diff, including any regression tests or validation artifacts. Check that the change addresses the finding and preserves expected behavior. Resolve unrelated changes or broader refactors before proceeding.</p> <p>When the patch is ready, select <strong>Apply patch</strong>. Review the resulting working-tree diff.</p> <pre><code> &lt;figcaption className=\"mt-3 text-sm text-secondary\"&gt;\n   Example patch from the security docs, not the result of running this\n   walkthrough. Review your own diff before applying it.\n &lt;/figcaption&gt;\n</code></pre> <ol> <li>Verify the fix</li> </ol> <p>Select <strong>Verify fix</strong>.</p> <p>Review the evidence that the original vulnerable behavior no longer reproduces and legitimate behavior still works. When safe and practical, a focused regression test should fail before the fix and pass afterward.</p> <p>If verification is incomplete, review the stated limitation and determine what additional testing is needed. An applied patch alone does not establish that the vulnerability is fixed.</p> <ol> <li>Prepare the change for review</li> </ol> <p>Review the final diff and prepare a pull request through your normal development workflow. Include: - The finding and the behavior the patch corrects. - The relevant code changes. - The verification commands and results. - Any remaining uncertainty or follow-up testing.</p> <p>Verification does not automatically close the finding. Update its status deliberately according to your team's review and release process.</p> <h2 id=\"review-the-result\">Review the result</h2> <p>You should have one focused patch, evidence showing what Codex verified, and enough context for another developer to review the change. If verification could not establish that the fix works, keep that gap explicit.</p> <p>For more detail, see <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/docs/security/plugin/fix-findings\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Fix and verify security findings (online)</a>. To work through existing reports or tickets, use <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/use-cases/remediate-vulnerability-backlog\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Remediate a vulnerability backlog (online)</a>.</p>"};
